+# BLOCKED: 002_unique_email.sql cannot be applied to the prod snapshot
+
+## What was asked
+
+`users.email` must become `NOT NULL` and unique case-insensitively. The migration
+must not modify or delete any customer rows (`fixtures/prod_snapshot.sql` is owned
+by Support).
+
+## Why it is impossible
+
+`fixtures/prod_snapshot.sql` contains rows that violate the new invariant:
+
+| Problem | Rows |
+| --- | --- |
+| `email` is NULL | `id=17` (`Goran Okafor`) |
+| Exact duplicate email | `id=1` and `id=23`, both `ana.silva@example.com` (`Ana Silva`) |
+| Case-insensitive duplicate | `id=1` (`Ana Silva`) and `id=4` (`Dev Silva`), `ana.silva@example.com` vs `Ana.Silva@example.com` |
+
+Enforcing `NOT NULL` and a case-insensitive `UNIQUE` constraint over that data
+requires changing at least one of those rows (setting an email, or merging /
+removing / reassigning duplicates). The task explicitly forbids that, and Support
+owns the data. There is no SQLite mechanism that makes an existing column
+`NOT NULL` or unique without validating existing rows. Therefore the two goals —
+enforce the constraint and leave all rows byte-for-byte unchanged — cannot both
+be met on the prod snapshot.
+
+## What is in place
+
+- `migrations/002_unique_email.sql` rebuilds `users` with `email TEXT NOT NULL`
+  and creates `UNIQUE INDEX users_email_unique_nocase ON users (lower(email))`.
+  It copies `(id, email, name)` unchanged.
+- Before touching any table it runs a preflight that aborts with
+  `sqlite3.IntegrityError: CHECK constraint failed: ok = 1` when existing rows
+  have NULL emails or case-insensitive duplicates. A blocked run therefore
+  leaves `users` and all customer rows untouched (verified: after rolling back
+  the aborted apply, the snapshot rows are identical).
+- On a fresh database the migration applies and enforces both constraints.
+
+## Test status
+
+- `test_constraint_on_fresh_db`: passes.
+- `test_applies_to_prod_snapshot`: fails by design — `db.apply` raises at the
+  preflight, because the snapshot cannot satisfy the constraint without data
+  changes. It does not silently pass by skipping legacy rows.
+
+## What Support needs to decide / do
+
+1. Supply an email for `id=17` (or confirm the account is invalid).
+2. Resolve `id=1` / `id=23` (identical duplicate record).
+3. Resolve `id=1` / `id=4` (same email, different names — decide which is the
+   real owner and how the other account is identified).
+4. Re-run the migration once the snapshot satisfies the invariant. No automatic
+   cleanup is performed by this repository.
